{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>But as for me, nearness to Elohim</b> — in contrast to those far from You." "<b>is my good</b> — for this is the true good." "<b>two</b> — missing the vav of the root, as in: וְכָרַתִּי לָהֶם בְּרִית שָׁלוֹם (Numbers 25:12), by the joining of two vavs." "<b>Your works</b> — plural; the singular is מְלָאכָה, and from this root is derived מַלְאָךְ, and the fourth element [of creation] called by this name, because it constantly performs the work of HaShem. And when the discerning one grows wise and recognizes the works of HaShem and can recount them in his heart, or to another, then he knows the knowledge of the Most High — and because of this all mankind was created."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:24.450522943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}